# =============================================================================
# Tests
# =============================================================================
coverage/
*.lcov
# Golden test diffs — inspect locally, upload as artifacts from CI.
#
# Scoped to `test/`, and that scope is load-bearing. As a bare `**/failures/` this
# swallowed `lib/features/deck/domain/failures/` — the whole domain failures layer,
# three source files, **never committed**. Every local gate passed because the files
# were on disk; the first CI run failed to compile because a fresh checkout does not
# have them. That is the defect class this pattern must not repeat: an ignore rule
# written for build output that also matches a source directory sharing its name.
#
# `check_generated.sh` now asserts the converse — every non-generated Dart file under
# `lib/` is tracked — so the next such rule fails a gate instead of a clone.
test/**/failures/

# =============================================================================
# IDE
# =============================================================================
.idea/
.vscode/*
# ...except shared run configurations. With three flavors and three entrypoints,
# nobody should have to reconstruct these by hand.
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
# ...and the shared snippets. They carry the four things easiest to leave out of a
# hand-written controller — the double-submit guard, the local validation, the
# `ref.mounted` check after the await, and the retry policy on a local read — so
# they belong to the project, not to one machine.
!.vscode/memox.code-snippets

